issue_context.body:
Hey there! 👋

I just created a new playwright project and called the following test. Can somebody explain why I can't use the performance api?

```bash
npm init playwright@latest new-project
```

```typescript
//example.spec.ts
import { test } from "@playwright/test";

test.beforeEach(async ({ page }) => {
  await page.goto("https://demo.playwright.dev/todomvc");
});

test.describe("New Todo", () => {
  test("should allow me to add todo items", async ({ page }) => {
    console.log(
      await page.evaluate(() => {
        window.performance.mark("start");
        window.performance.mark("end");
        return window.performance.measure("my-measure", "start", "end");
      })
    );
  });
});
```

This logs 'undefined' in every browser. Calling this within Chrome for example gives this expected result:

```javascript
{
    "name": "my-measure",
    "entryType": "measure",
    "startTime": 224071,
    "duration": 3577.699999988079
}
```

comments:
Found two bugs regarding serialisation, you can workaround it by passing the direct value instead of using the PerformanceMeasure class.

For later visiting:

a) isError() was throwing.
b) Object.keys() returns [] for the PerformanceMeasure class. toJSON would be nicer, but needs to be clarified.

